            <modifications expression="&quot;&lt;html>&lt;p>This example demonstrates a network of Boolean blocksfrom package &lt;a href=\&quot;modelica://Modelica.Blocks.MathBoolean\&quot;>Modelica.Blocks.MathBoolean&lt;/a>.&#xA;Note, that&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li> at the right side of the model, several MathBoolean.ShowValue blocks are present, that visualize the actual value of the respective Boolean signal in a diagram animation (\&quot;green\&quot; means \&quot;true\&quot;).&lt;/li>&lt;li> the Boolean values of the input and output signals are visualized in the diagram animation, by the small \&quot;circles\&quot; close to the connectors. If a \&quot;circle\&quot; is \&quot;white\&quot;, the signal is &lt;strong>false&lt;/strong>. If a \&quot;circle\&quot; is \&quot;green\&quot;, the signal is &lt;strong>true&lt;/strong>.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul>&lt;/html>&quot;" elementName="info"/>
          </annotations>
        </elements>
